     "explanation": "Every Wholehearted interviewee who described sustained joy also described an active, specific gratitude practice — not a passive feeling of thankfulness, but a repeated behavior like naming one concrete good thing daily. Avoidance and silent affirmations don't interrupt the bracing reflex because they don't anchor attention to the present moment. Waiting for enough good outcomes doesn't work either, since scarcity culture will always find the next reason to brace.",
