     "explanation": "Research on expert decision-making shows that intuition is fast, experience-based pattern recognition — professionals like veteran nurses or firefighters register a pattern their conscious mind hasn't finished analyzing and act on it. It isn't mystical and it isn't random; it's built from thousands of prior data points compressed into a feeling. Certainty culture dismisses this as unreliable simply because it can't be footnoted in the moment it occurs.",
