     "type": "application",
     "title": "Your Wholehearted Daily Practice Framework",
     "content": "**Morning (1 minute):** Name one specific thing you're grateful for before you check your phone. Say it out loud if you can.\n\n**Midday (2 minutes):** Pause once and ask your body one honest question: what do I actually need right now — rest, food, movement, quiet? Give it, even briefly, without earning it first.\n\n**Evening (3 minutes):** Journal two sentences: one moment today you showed courage or let yourself be seen, and one moment you offered yourself the same compassion you'd offer a friend.\n\n**Weekly (15 minutes, same day each week):** Review your notes for one pattern — numbing, comparison, foreboding joy, self-doubt. Just notice it. Noticing is the practice; fixing it instantly is not required.\n\n**Monthly (ongoing):** Choose one guidepost to be your deliberate focus — resilient spirit this month, creativity next month, meaningful work after that. Let the previous months' small anchors keep running quietly underneath the new one.\n\n**Yearly:** Expect to have rotated through all ten guideposts roughly once, none of them perfectly, none of them finished. Start the cycle again. That repetition, not any final state of enlightenment, is what Wholehearted living actually is. You are not behind. There is no finish line to be behind on — only a practice you either return to today, or don't.",
